WEBVTT

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.955
A flight price is only one part of a trip.
Travel

00:00:02.955 --> 00:00:07.290
Estimator brings transport, accommodation,
daily spending, extras, and a contingency
into

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:09.135
one explained planning budget.

00:00:09.465 --> 00:00:13.645
Base costs are illustrative estimates.
Configured providers can return dated flight

00:00:13.645 --> 00:00:17.580
quotes and venue information. The interface
distinguishes those sources instead of

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:20.190
presenting every number as a current booking
price.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.490
Before applying a flight, the server checks
who selected it, the

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:27.720
route, travel dates, and party size. A
selection older than fifteen

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:31.445
minutes must be refreshed. The browser cannot
simply invent verified quote

00:00:31.445 --> 00:00:32.525
metadata.

00:00:32.855 --> 00:00:35.720
For example, seven hundred dollars at an
assumed rate of two

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:39.355
hundred eighty Pakistani rupees becomes one
hundred ninety-six thousand rupees for

00:00:39.355 --> 00:00:42.635
a group. If it is a per-person fare, two
travellers double

00:00:42.635 --> 00:00:44.000
that flight amount.

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:48.210
The selected flight replaces the sample
transport line once. Other costs

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:52.930
remain. The subtotal and contingency are
recalculated, while baggage, transfers, and

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:55.370
seller fees still need separate confirmation.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:58.960
A provider may return no photos, no usable
offers, or a

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:03.010
quota error. The app explains that result. It
does not replace

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:06.110
missing live data with invented bargains. A
saved plan is a

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:08.400
snapshot, not a reservation.
